stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Recorded: Persist a unique intention
    Recorded --> Rejected: Invalid or blocked by policy
    Recorded --> Submitting: Reserve exposure and commit identity
    Submitting --> Rejected: Confirmed rejection
    Submitting --> Open: Confirmed resting order
    Submitting --> Partial: Confirmed partial fill with remainder open
    Submitting --> Filled: Confirmed complete fill
    Submitting --> Canceled: IOC remainder canceled
    Submitting --> Unknown: Timeout or ambiguous outcome
    Open --> Partial: Canonical fill applied once
    Open --> Filled: Remaining quantity filled
    Partial --> Partial: Additional unique fill
    Partial --> Filled: Remaining quantity filled
    Open --> CancelPending: Cancellation intention recorded
    Partial --> CancelPending: Cancellation intention recorded
    CancelPending --> Canceled: Cancellation confirmed
    CancelPending --> Filled: Fill wins the cancel race
    CancelPending --> Open: Cancel failed and order confirmed unfilled/open
    CancelPending --> Partial: Cancel failed and partial order remains open
    CancelPending --> Unknown: Outcome cannot be established
    Unknown --> Open: Reconciled open
    Unknown --> Partial: Reconciled partial/open
    Unknown --> Filled: Reconciled filled
    Unknown --> Canceled: Reconciled canceled
    Unknown --> Rejected: Confirmed no accepted order
    Unknown --> Unknown: Evidence insufficient / pause and retain reservation
    Rejected --> [*]
    Filled --> [*]
    Canceled --> [*]

    note right of Unknown
        Unknown is a durable nonterminal state.
        A timeout or one empty lookup is not proof of rejection.
        Operator review is required when reconciliation cannot resolve it.
    end note
    note right of Canceled
        Canceled orders can have nonzero filled quantity.
        Fill facts remain reconcilable after order termination.
        Terminal state never deletes execution history.
    end note
